Marked the invalid-profile and out-of-range paths as unlikely and split them so the common valid decode path stays straight-line. This reduces branch-layout overhead for the overwhelmingly valid lookups during decoding.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(profile == NULL, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    if (__builtin_expect(profileIndex >= profile->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```